# Copilot & Automation Agent Guide

This guide explains how Copilot and other automation agents interact with the theme scaffold.

## 1. Front Matter & Mustache Integration

- All `.mustache` files should have a YAML front matter block for Copilot.
- Key metadata: `title`, `version`, `slug`, `author`, `type`, `copilot_ready`.

## 2. Prompts, Instructions & Chatmodes

- See `.github/` for prompts, instructions, and chatmode templates.
- Link each prompt/instruction to the relevant doc or script.

## 3. Automation Workflow

- Copilot/agents should:
  - Detect all `.mustache` files.
  - Parse front matter and replace all placeholders.
  - Output production-ready theme files.
  - Validate that no placeholders remain.

## 4. Extending Automation

- When adding new automation, update this file and [repo-template.md](./repo-template.md).
- Document any new front matter fields or Copilot-specific requirements.

